claim.claim-text:
at least one stationary member (306);
an input member (302);
a plurality of planetary gearsets (308, 310, 312, 314) operatively coupled to the input member (302), each planetary gearset of the plurality of planetary gearsets including a sun gear (320, 330, 340, 350), a plurality of planet gears (324, 334, 344, 354) operatively coupled to the sun gear, a planet carrier (322, 332, 342, 352) operatively coupled to the plurality of planet gears, and a ring gear (326, 336, 346, 356) operatively coupled to the plurality of planet gears, the plurality of planetary gearsets including a first planetary gearset (308), a second planetary gearset (110, 310, 510), a third planetary gearset (312), and a fourth planetary gearset (314);
a plurality of selective couplers (362, 364, 366, 368, 370, 372) operatively coupled to the plurality of planetary gearsets, each of the plurality of selective couplers (362, 364, 366, 368, 370, 372) having an engaged configuration and a disengaged configuration, the plurality of selective couplers (362, 364, 366, 368, 370, 372) including a first number of clutches (366, 368, 370, 372) and a second number of brakes (362, 364), the first number being greater than the second number; and
an output member (304) operatively coupled to the input member (302) through the plurality of planetary gearsets, wherein the input member (302) is operatively coupled to the plurality of planetary gearsets only through a subset of the first number of clutches, the subset including a first clutch (366), a second clutch (368), and a third clutch (370), wherein
the first clutch (366), when engaged, fixedly couples the input member (302) to a first group of the plurality of planetary gearsets,
the second clutch (368), when engaged, fixedly couples the input member (302) to a second group of the plurality of planetary gearsets,
the third clutch (370), when engaged, fixedly couples the input member (302) to a third group of the plurality of planetary gearsets, and
each of the first planetary gearset (308), the second planetary gearset (310), the third planetary gearset (312), and the fourth planetary gearset (314) are included in at least one of the first group of the plurality of planetary gearsets, the second group of the plurality of planetary gearsets, and the third group of the plurality of planetary gearsets, wherein the first clutch (366), when engaged, fixedly couples the input member (302) to the planet carrier (332) of the second planetary gearset (310) and to the planet carrier (352) of the fourth planetary gearset (314); the second clutch (368), when engaged, fixedly couples the input member (302) to the planet carrier (322) of the first planetary gearset (308) and to the planet carrier (342) of the third planetary gearset (312); and the third clutch (370), when engaged, fixedly couples the input member (302) to the sun gear (340) of the third planetary gearset (312).

a first interconnector (380) which fixedly couples the sun gear (350) of the fourth planetary gearset (314), the ring gear (346) of the third planetary gearset (312), and the ring gear (336) of the second planetary gearset (310) together;
a second interconnector (382) which fixedly couples the planet carrier (332) of the second planetary gearset (310) to the planet carrier (352) of the fourth planetary gearset (314);
a third interconnector (384) which fixedly couples the sun gear (320) of the first planetary gearset (308) to the sun gear (330) of the second planetary gearset (310); and
a fourth interconnector (386) which fixedly couples the planet carrier (322) of the first planetary gearset (308) to the planet carrier (342) of the third planetary gearset (312) , wherein the plurality of selective couplers (162, 164, 166, 168, 170, 172, 362, 364, 366, 368, 370, 372, 562, 564, 566, 568, 570, 572) includes the first clutch (166, 366, 566), the second clutch (168, 368, 568), the third clutch (170, 370, 570), a fourth clutch (172, 372, 572), a first brake (162, 362, 562) fixedly coupled to the at least one stationary member (106, 306, 506), and a second brake (164, 364, 564) fixedly coupled to the at least one stationary member (106, 306, 506).

the first brake (362), when engaged, fixedly couples the sun gear (320) of the first planetary gearset (308) and the sun gear (330) of the second planetary gearset (310) to the at least one stationary member (306);
the second brake (364), when engaged, fixedly couples the ring gear (326) of the first planetary gearset (308) to the at least one stationary member (306);
the first clutch (366), when engaged, fixedly couples the input member (302) to the planet carrier (332) of the second planetary gearset (310) and to the planet carrier (352) of the fourth planetary gearset (314);
the second clutch (368), when engaged, fixedly couples the input member (302) to the planet carrier (322) of the first planetary gearset (308) and to the planet carrier (342) of the third planetary gearset (312);
the third clutch (370), when engaged, fixedly couples the input member (302) to the sun gear (340) of the third planetary gearset (312); and
the fourth clutch (372), when engaged, fixedly couples the ring gear (326) of the first planetary gearset (308) to the sun gear (340) of the third planetary gearset (312).

the input member (302) is accessible proximate the first end (316) of the housing;
the output member (304) is accessible proximate the second end (318) of the housing;
the first planetary gearset (308) is positioned between the first end (316) of the housing and the second planetary gearset (310);
the second planetary gearset (310) is positioned between the first planetary gearset (308) and the third planetary gearset (312);
the third planetary gearset (312) is positioned between the second planetary gearset (310) and the fourth planetary gearset (314); and
the fourth planetary gearset (314) is positioned between the third planetary gearset (312) and the second end (318) of the housing.
